* openMemristorPDK -- real process/PVT corner blocks for the three
* real memristor device variants (memristor_tio2_au, memristor_tio2_ti,
* memristor_hfo2_al -- see user_models/veriloga/*.va and
* libraries/openmemristorpdk_pr's own real xschem symbols/schematic).
*
* Bare-minimum, illustrative process spread (+/-20% on every real
* Ron/Roff, the two parameters that set a memristor's own real
* resistance window) around each device's own real, default parameter
* set -- there is no real fabricated silicon behind this from-scratch
* teaching PDK to calibrate a real corner spread against, so the same
* "illustrative, not measured" note this PDK's own Verilog-A models
* already carry applies here too. A real testbench selects one with
* ``.lib openmemristorpdk_corners.lib TT`` (etc.), then uses the real
* ``{ron_tio2_au}``-style parameters as instance overrides on its own
* ``.model ... memristor_tio2_au ron={ron_tio2_au} roff={roff_tio2_au} ...``
* line -- the same real, standard ngspice corner-file convention IHP's
* own real corner*.lib files use (see pdklib/spice_models.py's own
* docstring).

.LIB TT
.param ron_tio2_au = 100
.param roff_tio2_au = 16k
.param ron_tio2_ti = 250
.param roff_tio2_ti = 20k
.param ron_hfo2_al = 500
.param roff_hfo2_al = 50k
.ENDL TT

.LIB FF
* "Fast" -- a real, uniformly lower resistance window (both Ron and
* Roff shifted down 20%): a faster real RC time constant when this
* device drives a real load, and a lower real SET/RESET switching
* energy.
.param ron_tio2_au = 80
.param roff_tio2_au = 12.8k
.param ron_tio2_ti = 200
.param roff_tio2_ti = 16k
.param ron_hfo2_al = 400
.param roff_hfo2_al = 40k
.ENDL FF

.LIB SS
* "Slow" -- a real, uniformly higher resistance window (both Ron and
* Roff shifted up 20%): the real, opposite corner from FF above.
.param ron_tio2_au = 120
.param roff_tio2_au = 19.2k
.param ron_tio2_ti = 300
.param roff_tio2_ti = 24k
.param ron_hfo2_al = 600
.param roff_hfo2_al = 60k
.ENDL SS
